=begin

  Logs raw XML output to <Lich log folder>\<game code>-<char name>\<year>\<month>\<date>_<time>.xml
  (the Lich log folder is LOG_DIR, set by Lich's --logs= option, or lich\logs;
  a file started by a new day or a full file whose name is already taken ends in _01, _02, ... before .xml;
  a restarted logger appends to a file of the same name)
  starts a new file after 30,000 lines (somewhere around 1mb)

  SYNTAX:  ;logxml
           ;logxml --timestamp="%F %T %Z"
           ;logxml --rnum                    - Lich ID on room titles (loads the map in the background if nothing has)
           ;autostart add --global logxml --timestamp=\"%F %T %Z\" --rnum
           log format based on https://apidock.com/ruby/DateTime/strftime

  Shamelessly stolen and slightly altered (to use XML) from Tillmen's log script.

  Messages from the client will be wrapped in <!-- CLIENT -->...<!-- ENDCLIENT --> tags.

       author: elanthia-online
 contributors: LostRanger, Xanlin, Tysong
         game: gs
      version: 0.6.6
     required: Lich >= 5.14.0

  changelog:
    0.6.6 (2026-11-10):
      * drop the start-up checks for an old Lich and for script trust, which can no longer fail (Lich 5.14.0 or later and Ruby 4 are already required)
    0.6.5 (2026-11-10):
      * when typed commands stop being logged after an error, the logger echoes the error, the file and line where it happened, and how to restart it with the same options, and the log file gets a line saying typed commands are not logged after it
      * a log file that cannot be closed goes to the Lich log with its path and the error, instead of a bare "Can't close file!"
    0.6.4 (2026-11-10):
      * the reget lines at the top of the log no longer end in a stray carriage return, and an empty reget writes no blank line
      * logs go to Lich's log folder (LOG_DIR, set by Lich's --logs= option), or LICH_DIR/logs when it is not set
      * a log file now also gets its footer when the logger is stopped (;kill, logout, Lich exiting), not only when a new file starts; a footer that cannot be written then goes to the Lich log
      * a log file whose header cannot be written is closed instead of being left open
      * the first line after midnight goes into the new day's file (it went into yesterday's)
      * only lines written to the file count toward the 30,000, so skipped stream lines no longer cut a file short
      * a file started by a new day or a full file whose name is taken (for example, a whole file within one second) gets an _01, _02, ... suffix (sorting after the first file) instead of being appended to it; the first file of a run still appends to a file of the same name
      * after a full file, the next file is opened when its first line comes, so no file is left without lines when that line comes after midnight or the logger stops first
    0.6.3 (2026-11-10):
      * --rnum finds the Lich room number in the map's UID table, never by matching the room from the logger (no LOCATION/PEER sent, no "no map database found" in the log)
      * --rnum writes no " - ]" when the room has no Lich number
      * --rnum loads the map once in the background when nothing has loaded it yet (in DragonRealms, Lich's own room display does not load it by default)
      * needs Lich 5.14.0 or later (Map.loaded?)
    0.6.2 (2026-11-10):
      * log_timestamp on with no usable log_timestamp_format echoes and uses "%F %T %Z" instead of crashing
      * an empty --timestamp= echoes and is ignored instead of writing blank timestamps
    0.6.1 (2026-10-29):
      * fix --timestamp being ignored unless its value was wrapped in quotes
      * use --timestamp format for log file header/footer lines when enabled
    0.6.0 (2024-09-10):
      * add --rnum support
    0.5.0 (2023-03-31):
      * Rubocop code cleanup
      * Adjust filename to include hours, minutes, seconds
      * Save into subdirectories by year/month
      * Starts a new file when the day changes
      * Add log timestamp CLI option for non-DragonRealms
    0.4.1 (2019-12-28):
      * Implement 0.4, correctly.
    0.4 (2019-12-28):
      * ';logxml streams' will now include pushStream and popStream messages.  Note that this may be very, very noisy
        due to room window updates and such.
    0.3 (2017-04-24):
      * fix output including both XML and plaintext from downstream.
    0.2 (2017-04-23):
      * Indicate where full logging started in the log file (as opposed to contents from regetall).  Client data before
        this point can't be fully logged due to Lich not loading the script in time, so yell about it.
      * Use a more configuration-safe mechanism of complaining about not being trusted.  Also, explain why trust is
        needed.
=end

hide_me
if defined?(get_settings)
  settings = get_settings
  stamp_enable = settings.log_timestamp
  stamp_format = settings.log_timestamp_format
end
Script.current.want_script_output = false
Script.current.want_upstream = true
Script.current.want_downstream = false
Script.current.want_downstream_xml = true

if Script.current.vars[0] =~ /--timestamp="([^"]*)"/
  stamp_option = Regexp.last_match[1]
elsif (stamp_arg = Script.current.vars[1..].to_a.find { |v| v.start_with?('--timestamp=') })
  stamp_option = stamp_arg.delete_prefix('--timestamp=')
end

# Only a non-empty String is handed to strftime as a format (as in log.lic).
if stamp_option.is_a?(String) && !stamp_option.empty?
  stamp_format = stamp_option
  stamp_enable = true
else
  echo 'timestamp was given without a format, so it is ignored; to add timestamps use --timestamp="%F %T %Z".' unless stamp_option.nil?
  if stamp_enable && !(stamp_format.is_a?(String) && !stamp_format.empty?)
    echo "log_timestamp is on in your settings, but log_timestamp_format #{stamp_format.inspect} is not a format; using \"%F %T %Z\"."
    stamp_format = '%F %T %Z'
  end
end

show_room_numbers = false
if Script.current.vars[0] =~ /\-\-(?:roomnum|rnum)/
  show_room_numbers = true
end

log_streams = Script.current.vars.include?("streams")

# The Lich room number for --rnum comes from the map's UID table, which is
# empty until something loads the map, and in DragonRealms Lich's own room
# display does not by default. Load it once, off the get loop below: the
# load sends no game command but can take seconds, long enough for lich-5's
# 200-line downstream buffer to drop lines during a login burst.
if show_room_numbers && !Map.loaded?
  Thread.new {
    begin
      echo 'no map database could be loaded, so --rnum adds no Lich room numbers.' unless Map.load
    rescue StandardError => e
      echo "the map failed to load (#{e.message}), so --rnum adds no Lich room numbers."
    end
  }
end

# Typed commands go onto the downstream buffer, so the get loop below logs
# them in order with the game lines. When this thread stops on an error, it
# says why (the error, its file and line, and how to restart with the same
# arguments) and leaves a notice line in the log file (as in log.lic): the
# game lines are still logged, the commands no longer are. Thread#kill
# (;kill, logout) stops it without either, and so does a StopIteration from
# upstream_get or the push: loop rescues that one itself and ends. lich-5's
# upstream_get does not raise it.
Thread.new {
  begin
    loop {
      Script.current.downstream_buffer.push "<!-- CLIENT -->#{upstream_get}<!-- ENDCLIENT -->"
    }
  rescue StandardError => e
    reason = "#{e.class}: #{e.message.to_s.gsub(/\s+/, ' ').strip}"
    # The file and line, without the directory, which keeps the echo short.
    frame = e.backtrace&.first
    where = frame && ((match = frame.match(/\A(.+?):(\d+)/)) ? "#{File.basename(match[1])}:#{match[2]}" : frame)
    script = Script.current
    restart = [";#{script.name}", script.vars&.first.to_s.strip].reject(&:empty?).join(' ')
    echo "typed commands are no longer logged: the upstream thread stopped on #{reason}#{" at #{where}" if where}. " \
         "Game lines are still logged; restart the logger (;kill #{script.name}, then #{restart}) to log typed commands again."
    # A "-" before another "-" is spaced out: "--" would end the comment
    # early and is not allowed in an XML comment. The ")" keeps a last "-"
    # off the closing "-->".
    script.downstream_buffer.push "<!-- logxml: typed commands are not logged after this line; the upstream thread stopped (#{reason.gsub(/-(?=-)/, '- ')}) -->"
  end
}

# Lich's LOG_DIR (set by Lich's --logs= option; pilepull.lic reads the
# logs there), or LICH_DIR/logs when it is not defined or empty.
log_root = (LOG_DIR if defined?(LOG_DIR)).to_s
log_root = File.join(LICH_DIR, 'logs') if log_root.empty?

started = false
# The line that opens the next file. A line read after midnight belongs to
# the new day's file: it is kept here while the old file is closed. After a
# full file, the next line is read before the next file is opened, so a file
# never waits with no line and then, when that line comes after midnight,
# is left under the old day with only its header and footer (as in log.lic).
carried_line = nil
loop {
  carried_line = get if started && carried_line.nil?
  dir = File.join(log_root, "#{XMLData.game}-#{XMLData.name}", Time.now.strftime("%Y"), Time.now.strftime("%m"))
  FileUtils.mkdir_p(dir) unless File.exist?(dir)
  thisdate = Time.now.strftime("%Y-%m-%d")
  stem = File.join(dir, Time.now.strftime("%Y-%m-%d_%H-%M-%S"))
  filename = "#{stem}.xml"
  # The first file keeps its name even when it exists (appended to); a new
  # file started within the same second gets "_01", "_02", ... instead, which
  # sorts after the first file's name (as in log.lic).
  if started
    suffix = 0
    filename = "#{stem}_#{format('%02d', suffix += 1)}.xml" while File.exist?(filename)
  end
  file = File.open(filename, 'a')
  header_written = false
  finished = false
  # Header, lines and footer in one begin/ensure: an error in the header
  # still closes the file, and the footer is written exactly once, also
  # when the logger stops (;kill, logout, Lich exiting).
  begin
    file.sync = true
    if stamp_enable
      file.puts "#{Time.now.strftime(stamp_format)}\n"
    else
      file.puts "#{Time.now.strftime("%Y-%m-%d %I:%M%P").sub(/0([0-9]+\:)/) { "#{$1}" }}\n"
    end
    header_written = true
    unless started
      if (Time.now - $login_time) < 30
        # lich-5's reget answers nil for an empty buffer (puts(nil) wrote a
        # blank line), and each line keeps the server's "\r" line end.
        Array(reget).each { |line| file.puts line.chomp }
        file.puts "<!-- Above contents from reget; full logging now active -->\n"
      end

      echo "XML Logging started, currently logging to #{filename}"
      started = true
    end

    # Only lines written to the file count toward the 30000.
    written = 0
    while written < 30000
      line = carried_line || get
      carried_line = nil
      # The date is checked before the line is written, so the first line
      # of a new day starts its file.
      if Time.now.strftime("%Y-%m-%d") != thisdate
        carried_line = line
        break
      end
      if show_room_numbers && line =~ /^<resource picture=.*roomName/
        # The Lich room number comes only from the map's UID table, as in
        # log.lic: Map.current would match the room from this script's
        # thread, which can send LOCATION or PEER and clear its buffer. A
        # UID with no single mapped room (or no map loaded) adds no number.
        room_ids = Map.ids_from_uid(XMLData.room_id)
        room_number = room_ids.size == 1 ? " - #{room_ids.first}" : ''
        if XMLData.game =~ /^GS/
          line.sub!(']') { "#{room_number}] (u#{XMLData.room_id})" }
        elsif !room_number.empty?
          line.sub!(']') { "#{room_number}]" }
        end
      end
      next unless log_streams or line !~ /^<(?:push|pop)Stream/

      if stamp_enable
        file.puts "#{Time.now.strftime("#{stamp_format}")}: #{line}"
      else
        file.puts line
      end
      written += 1
    end
    finished = true
  ensure
    begin
      if header_written
        begin
          if stamp_enable
            file.puts "#{Time.now.strftime(stamp_format)}\n"
          else
            file.puts "#{Time.now.strftime("%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S.%L %:z")}\n"
          end
        rescue IOError, SystemCallError => e
          # A file closed for the next one raises as before; when an error
          # or ;kill (Thread#kill) is stopping the logger, the failed footer
          # goes to the Lich log instead of replacing the reason it stopped.
          raise if finished

          Lich.log "logxml: the footer of #{file.path} was not written while the logger stopped (#{e.class}: #{e.message})"
        end
      end
    ensure
      begin
        file.close
      rescue StandardError => e
        Lich.log "logxml: closing the log file #{filename} failed (#{e.class}: #{e.message}); lines are written as they come, with sync on, but the file may be missing its footer or a last write"
      end
    end
  end
}
